<article class="env-definition" id="FF9854">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/FF9854">Definition <span data-tag="FF9854">2.3.4.1</span>.</a>$n$-category Let $\calC $ be a simplicial set and $n \geq -1$ an integer. We will say that $\calC $ is an <em>$n$-category</em> if it is an $\infty $-category and the following additional conditions are satisfied: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
Given a pair of maps $f, f': \Delta ^ n \rightarrow \calC $, if $f$ and $f'$ are homotopic relative to $\bd \Delta ^ n$, then $f = f'$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
Given $m > n$ and a pair of maps $f,f': \Delta ^ m \rightarrow \calC $, if $f | \bd \Delta ^ m = f' | \bd \Delta ^ m$, then $f = f'$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>